+# Security policy for The Daily Grind site
+
+This document records the client-side security audit of the site and how the
+resulting policies are deployed and maintained.
+
+## Audit summary (2026-10-28)
+
+| Area | Finding | Fix |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Scripts | No `<script>` tags, inline handlers, or DOM sinks exist. | Strict nonce-based CSP so none can be injected. |
+| Styles | One inline `<style>` block and one `style=""` attribute. | Moved to `/styles.css`; `style-src 'self'`. |
+| Images | Hero background hot-links `images.unsplash.com`. | `img-src` limited to that origin; referrer stripped. |
+| Logout | `/logout` was a GET link, triggerable cross-site. | POST-only form, `Clear-Site-Data`, Fetch Metadata. |
+| Headers | Server sent no security headers at all. | Full header set below on every response. |
+| Server | Every path, including `/styles.css`, returned the HTML page. | Explicit static allowlist with correct `Content-Type`. |
+
+## Response headers
+
+Every response from `server.js` carries (see `security-headers.js`):
+
+```http
+Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'nonce-<random>' 'strict-dynamic' 'report-sample'; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self' https://images.unsplash.com; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; form-action 'self'; base-uri 'none'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'self'; require-trusted-types-for 'script'; report-to csp-endpoint; report-uri /csp-report
+Reporting-Endpoints: csp-endpoint="/csp-report"
+Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin-allow-popups
+Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin
+X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
+X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
+Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
+Permissions-Policy: camera=(), geolocation=(), microphone=(), focus-without-user-activation=()
+Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=300; includeSubDomains
+Vary: Sec-Fetch-Dest, Sec-Fetch-Mode, Sec-Fetch-Site
+```
+
+Additionally, `/logout` responds with `Clear-Site-Data: "cookies", "storage", "cache"`,
+and the server rejects cross-site requests that are not plain top-level
+navigations (Fetch Metadata resource isolation) before any other handling.
+
+## Rules for changing the site
+
+- **Scripts**: must be same-origin and carry `nonce="{{CSP_NONCE}}"`. The
+  server swaps in a per-request value. Scripts loaded by a nonced script
+  inherit trust through `'strict-dynamic'`. Never add host or `https:`
+  allowlists to `script-src`.
+- **DOM sinks**: Trusted Types is enforced. Use `textContent`, `setHTML()`, or
+  a named `trustedTypes.createPolicy()` that actually sanitises. Add the policy
+  name to a `trusted-types` directive when you add one.
+- **Styles**: edit `styles.css`. No `<style>` blocks or `style=""` attributes.
+- **New third-party origins**: add them to the matching directive in
+  `security-headers.js` and, for versioned scripts or stylesheets, pin the URL
+  and add `integrity` + `crossorigin="anonymous"`.
+- **State-changing endpoints**: POST only. Set session cookies as
+  `__Host-<name>=...; Secure; HttpOnly; SameSite=Lax; Path=/`.
+
+## Rollout notes
+
+1. **HSTS**: `HSTS_MAX_AGE` defaults to 300 seconds. After confirming HTTPS
+   works for every subdomain, raise it in steps to `31536000`; `preload` is
+   appended automatically at that value.
+2. **CSP reports**: violations are logged by the `/csp-report` handler with
+   query strings removed and samples truncated to 40 characters. Review the
+   logs after deploying; ignore low-volume noise from extensions and old
+   browsers, and investigate repeated reports from modern user agents.
+3. **Trying a stricter change**: duplicate the header as
+   `Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only` with the proposed value, watch
+   reports, then promote it.
+4. **Production over HTTPS**: consider adding `upgrade-insecure-requests` to
+   the CSP once the site is only ever served over TLS.
+
+## Verification
+
+```sh
+npm run build   # syntax checks
+npm test        # policy unit tests, no server is started
+```
